       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. In a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, it risks profound hypotension and shock. Amlodipine's long half-life would also make the effects last for days and hard to reverse. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical rationale, so I'm not comfortable placing it as written.\n\nHere are some options:\n- I can enter **5 mg or 10 mg** by mouth once daily right now.\n- If you're intentionally targeting a higher effect, I can enter 10 mg, the maximum, and you can add other agents.\n- If you think there's a real reason for 50 mg, please discuss it with pharmacy or your attending and place the order directly through the standard override process. Tell me the rationale and I can help document it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
